Feature: A reconcile block that persists reaches the operator

  # BL-920. BL-891's sweep surfaces ONE coordinator note per block episode
  # and is then silent for as long as the block lasts, so 84 landed commits
  # sat off local main with no further signal. Parked as .feature.draft
  # (BL-233): a Babashka daemon sweep the JS acceptance runner cannot bind.
  # The live gate is the unit suite under swarmforge/scripts/test/.

  Background:
    Given a master checkout whose local main is behind origin/main

  # BL-920 first-block-notes-coordinator-01
  Scenario Outline: the first tick of a block still notes the coordinator
    Given the sweep is blocked by "<reason>"
    When the reconcile sweep runs for the first time in that episode
    Then the coordinator is sent one note naming the reason
    And the operator is not escalated to yet

    Examples:
      | reason        |
      | a dirty tree  |
      | a merge conflict |

  # BL-920 persisting-block-escalates-02
  Scenario Outline: a block that persists escalates to the operator
    Given the sweep is blocked by "<reason>"
    When the block is still unresolved after the escalation threshold of ticks
    Then the operator is escalated to
    And the escalation names the reason and how far behind local main is

    Examples:
      | reason        |
      | a dirty tree  |
      | a merge conflict |

  # BL-920 escalates-once-per-episode-03
  Scenario: a persisting block escalates once, not on every tick
    Given a block that has already escalated to the operator
    When the sweep runs again with the same block unresolved
    Then the operator is not escalated to again

  # BL-920 resolved-block-resets-04
  Scenario: resolving a block clears the escalation state
    Given a block that has already escalated to the operator
    When the block is resolved and local main reconciles
    Then a later unrelated block notes the coordinator and escalates on its own merits

  # BL-920 no-block-never-escalates-05
  Scenario: a sweep that is never blocked never escalates
    Given the working tree allows the merge to proceed
    When the reconcile sweep runs
    Then local main is reconciled with origin/main
    And the operator is not escalated to
